{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat → 52.7% acc, 0.85 GPU hrs), evidence is extremely sparse. The most impactful architectural uncertainty is whether multiprofile processing (capturing temporal/dynamic cellular information) provides a meaningful boost over singleprofile. config_010 isolates this variable: it keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat) as the baseline, changing only profile_setting to multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool). This cleanly tests whether multiprofile helps before committing to more expensive aggregation strategies (transformer) or heavier encoders (scgpt, ViT-L). If multiprofile + avgpool shows a clear improvement, subsequent experiments can exploit that direction with transformer aggregation or better encoders. Expected cost: modestly higher than config_009 (~1.3–1.7 GPU hrs) due to processing multiple profiles and avgpool, but still in the cheaper tier compared to ViT-L or transformer-based configs."
}

